modules: modules/lib_core
flags: -O

--- OUT --->
42
42
--- IR --->
# **the assertion is that neither call is left**, for two callees that reach the inliner by different routes.
#
# `tripled` is `#[inline]`, so its body was copied into this unit and the inliner would see it however the
# units were arranged. `doubled` is an ordinary external definition living in modcore's unit, and it is
# inlinable here only because every unit is merged into one llvm::Module before the O3 pipeline runs.
#
# that merge is why `-O` deliberately does not use the module object cache: cached objects are per-module, and
# handing the optimizer one unit at a time would turn `doubled` into a `declare` it cannot inline. If this
# case ever starts failing on the `doubled` line, the merge was skipped for an optimized build.
CHECK: i32 @main()
CHECK-NOT: call i32 @_modcore_tripled
CHECK-NOT: call i32 @_modcore_doubled
CHECK: ret i32 0
